<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
I immediately thought of Shato when I read this.  Can we say What the F***?!?!<P>*****<P>Invoke Death, our level 49 pet spell, seems to have been modified.<P>Up until the last patch, the spell would summon a skeleton between level 37 and 41. It now summons a skeleton between level 36 and 39. The base damage of the max summon (39) is still 55, the 36er hits for 49, 37th for 51, 38th for 53. Previously the base damage was 55 for the 41st, etc.<P>As such, while the damage output of the pets may look the same, I suspect they are now doing meaningfully less damage to level 45+ NPCs due to skill cap issues. I haven't done enough testing to confirm whether or not the relative HP values have been changed, nor done any parsing to see if they are being hit any harder by mobs of comparable level, and I probably won't be able to as I've had "other hits" off for far too long.<P>I did not cast Cackling Bones, however I would imagine the level of summoned pets for that spell has been shifted down as well. I suspect this change was related to the fact that the 44 and 49 pet summoned relatively high compared to all our previous pets and later pets (which would typically go green as we got the next level spell, whereas the best 49 pet was level 41 and thus still blue to a level 55.<P>Perhaps this is the Vision Approved method of making people actually want to use Minion of Shadows. Minion and Servant still seem to work the same. Mage and shaman pet spells still seem to work as before, as well.<P>I would appreciate other people testing this. I'd like to think I was just going more insane. <P>*****<P>I think its about time to give up on being the necro I used to be.  <IMG SRC="frown.gif" border="0"><P>--------------------<P>Lownar Baardeth - 54th Level Gnecromancer<BR>Kalaan - 30th Level Rogue<BR>Bertox. Server<P>Sendil- 50th Level Rogue<BR>Solusek Ro Server
</FONT>
